            <ArticleTitle>[Reintervention of myocardial revascularization by left thoracotomy in deep hypothermia. A clinical case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>325-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herewith we report a case of redo coronary-surgery which was approached through a left thoracotomy and in hypothermic arrest so as to avoid either a demanding dissection with its potential consequences over the functioning grafts and aortic cross-clamping thus making unnecessary any cardioplegia delivery. We describe the surgical procedure and analyze its advantages with respect to the usual median sternotomy approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
